1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:03,400
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,200
I'm Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,080
This is my little brother,
George.

4
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,240
[SNORTS]

5
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,440
This is Mommy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,799
And this is Daddy Pig.
[SNORTS]

7
00:00:12,799 --> 00:00:14,200
[LAUGHTER]

8
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,760
Peppa Pig.
[SNORTS]

9
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,960
[♪♪♪]

10
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,640
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

11
00:00:25,439 --> 00:00:27,119
[SNORTS]

12
00:00:27,119 --> 00:00:30,080
NARRATOR:
Mommy Pig has made
a special box for Peppa.

13
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:33,360
[SNORTS]
Peppa, this box
is just for you.

14
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:35,160
Thank you,
Mommy.

15
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:38,600
MOMMY PIG:
It's a secret box for you
to keep secret things in.

16
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,120
[SNORTS]
What things can I put in it,
Mommy?

17
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,040
Ho, ho. Only you
can decide that, Peppa.

18
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:45,800
It's your secret box.

19
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:49,199
[SNORTS]
I know what I can
put in it!

20
00:00:49,199 --> 00:00:51,280
Good. But don't tell me.
[SNORTS]

21
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:55,239
I won't tell you,
or George or Daddy.

22
00:00:55,239 --> 00:00:57,839
It's a secret.

23
00:00:57,839 --> 00:00:59,320
[♪♪♪]

24
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:02,080
George, this is
my secret box.

25
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:03,720
[SNORTS]
It's empty.

26
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:07,520
I have to find some things
to put inside.

27
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,280
[GIGGLES, SNORTS]

28
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:11,000
NARRATOR:
George wants to help Peppa.

29
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,479
[SNORTS]
No, George, only I must know
what's in the box.

30
00:01:15,479 --> 00:01:17,280
You have to wait outside

31
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,119
while I choose.

32
00:01:19,119 --> 00:01:21,800
[SNORTS]
[GIGGLING]

33
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:24,360
NARRATOR:
Peppa is going to choose
some secret things

34
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,600
to put in the box.

35
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:27,679
[PEPPA CONTINUES GIGGLING]

36
00:01:29,119 --> 00:01:31,759
[SNORTS]
Now my secret box
is full.

37
00:01:31,759 --> 00:01:33,280
[RATTLES]

38
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:36,759
George, you must not
look inside.

39
00:01:36,759 --> 00:01:40,520
NARRATOR:
George would like to know what
is inside Peppa's secret box.

40
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:43,839
If you like,
you can try to guess.

41
00:01:43,839 --> 00:01:44,960
[SNORTS]

42
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:47,160
[RATTLES]
Dine-Saw!

43
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,880
NARRATOR:
George thinks Peppa has put
a dinosaur in the box.

44
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:55,399
Oh, George! You always say
dinosaur for everything.

45
00:01:55,399 --> 00:02:00,440
[SNORTS]
Anyway, a dinosaur is too big
to fit in the box.

46
00:02:00,440 --> 00:02:04,240
NARRATOR:
George cannot guess what
is in Peppa's secret box.

47
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,960
Daddy Pig
is cleaning a picture.

48
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,919
Daddy!
This is my secret box.

49
00:02:09,919 --> 00:02:11,519
Mommy made it for me.

50
00:02:11,519 --> 00:02:14,799
[SNORTS]
It's very nice, Peppa.
What's inside?

51
00:02:14,799 --> 00:02:16,480
It's a secret.

52
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:20,280
[SNORTS]
George tried to guess,
but he didn't get it right.

53
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,000
Can I have a try?
[SNORTS]

54
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,079
Yes!

55
00:02:23,079 --> 00:02:24,400
[♪♪♪]

56
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,720
[RATTLES]

57
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:28,440
Hm. Have you put
my glasses inside?

58
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:33,239
No! Hee, hee! Your glasses
are on your head!

59
00:02:33,239 --> 00:02:34,359
So they are!

60
00:02:34,359 --> 00:02:36,200
[SNORTS]
Silly Daddy!

61
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:38,359
You must have
a proper guess.

62
00:02:38,359 --> 00:02:40,000
Okay.
[SNORTS]

63
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,720
Have you put Mommy's shoes
in the box?

64
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:45,120
Nope. And that's
all your guesses, used up.

65
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,640
NARRATOR:
Peppa likes secrets.

66
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:48,200
[♪♪♪]

67
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,440
Mommy!
[SNORTS]

68
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:51,920
No one knows
what is in my box.

69
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:53,160
[RATTLES]
[SNORTS]

70
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:55,440
Oh.
What has George got?

71
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:57,640
[SNORTS]
I made a box
for George too.

72
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:59,600
And he's filled it
with secret things.

73
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,880
And only George knows
what's inside.

74
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:03,120
[RATTLES]

75
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,959
Oh.

76
00:03:04,959 --> 00:03:08,000
NARRATOR:
Peppa would like to know
what is inside George's box.

77
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,600
[SNORTS]
It's George's toy dinosaur,

78
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,519
of course.
No!

79
00:03:12,519 --> 00:03:15,600
NARRATOR:
George's toy dinosaur
is not in George's box.

80
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:18,280
Hee-hee-hee!
It's too difficult!

81
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:20,160
[SNORTS]
I'll never guess.

82
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:23,200
NARRATOR:
Peppa does not like secrets
as much as she used to.

83
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:26,560
Maybe, if you showed George
one thing from your box,

84
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:28,519
then he could show you
one thing from his.

85
00:03:28,519 --> 00:03:30,160
Okay.
[SNORTS]

86
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:32,880
But we must do it
at the same time.

87
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:34,519
That's a good idea.

88
00:03:34,519 --> 00:03:38,079
On the count of three, you each
show what's in your boxes.

89
00:03:38,079 --> 00:03:39,920
Ready?
Yes.

90
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:43,280
One... two...
three.

91
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,160
NARRATOR: George has a drum... 
[CHUCKLES]

92
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:47,720
...and Peppa has a trumpet. 
[GIGGLES]

93
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:49,799
[PLAYING INSTRUMENTS]

94
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,760
Ho, ho! Lovely!

95
00:03:53,760 --> 00:03:55,720
Yes, it sounds very nice.

96
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:57,640
Do you have any more
secret things?

97
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:59,320
[GIGGLES, SNORTS]

98
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:01,679
NARRATOR
George has
a custard doughnut.

99
00:04:01,679 --> 00:04:03,000
Oh.

100
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,399
NARRATOR
But Peppa's box is empty.

101
00:04:05,399 --> 00:04:07,280
I've got nothing else.

102
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:10,519
Luckily, I have.
Come on, tuck in.

103
00:04:10,519 --> 00:04:13,079
NARRATOR:
George, Peppa, Mommy Pig
and Daddy Pig

104
00:04:13,079 --> 00:04:15,000
all like custard doughnuts.

105
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,079
I don't have a special box.

106
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:20,479
But I know a very good place
to hide my custard doughnut.

107
00:04:20,479 --> 00:04:23,400
Can you guess where?
Hm...

108
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:26,479
Are you going to hide it
in the fridge?

109
00:04:26,479 --> 00:04:28,000
No.
[SNORTS]

110
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,760
Somewhere much more special.

111
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:30,960
My tummy.

112
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,159
[MUNCHES]

113
00:04:32,159 --> 00:04:34,159
Mm! Delicious!

114
00:04:34,159 --> 00:04:35,320
[GIGGLES]

115
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:38,479
I'm going to hide mine
in my tummy.

116
00:04:38,479 --> 00:04:39,880
Me too.

117
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:41,039
[SNORTS]

118
00:04:41,039 --> 00:04:42,960
[ALL LAUGHING AND SNORTING]

119
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,960
[♪♪♪]

120
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:54,120
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

121
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:58,280
NARRATOR:
It is a bright, sunny day.

122
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,560
Peppa and her family
are in the park.

123
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,719
[SNORTS]

124
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:05,000
NARRATOR:
They are going to fly a kite.

125
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,719
[LAUGHING]

126
00:05:07,719 --> 00:05:10,960
NARRATOR:
George is going to fly
the kite first.

127
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,520
[SNORTS]

128
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,760
NARRATOR:
George runs as fast as he can.

129
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:18,640
But the kite won't fly.

130
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:20,719
[PANTING]

131
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:25,640
George, you're
doing it all wrong!

132
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:30,440
[SNORTS]
You didn't run fast enough.

133
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:32,560
Now it's my turn.

134
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:34,320
NARRATOR:
Peppa runs as fast as she can.

135
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:36,400
[GIGGLING]

136
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:39,800
NARRATOR:
But the kite still won't fly.

137
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:41,840
[PANTING]

138
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:48,919
[SNORTS]
The kite won't fly
if there isn't any wind,

139
00:05:48,919 --> 00:05:50,880
no matter how fast
you run.

140
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:52,080
Oh.

141
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,520
[SNORTS]
We just have to wait,

142
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:56,000
until the wind
picks up a bit.

143
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,200
Oh.

144
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:58,840
[LEAVES RUSTLING]

145
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:02,960
Look!
It's getting windy.

146
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:06,000
NARRATOR:
Now that it is windy,
the kite can fly.

147
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,159
[LAUGHING]

148
00:06:07,159 --> 00:06:09,479
[SNORTS, LAUGHING]

149
00:06:09,479 --> 00:06:13,120
NARRATOR:
The wind is quite strong now.

150
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:15,520
The wind is very strong now. 
[CONTINUES LAUGHING]

151
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:18,200
George!
Ha-ha-ha!

152
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,400
[CRIES]

153
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:20,599
Peppa!

154
00:06:20,599 --> 00:06:21,799
Thank you, Daddy.

155
00:06:21,799 --> 00:06:23,120
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE LAUGH]

156
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,760
NARRATOR:
Daddy Pig flies the kite.

157
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:27,240
Hooray!
[ALL LAUGH]

158
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:29,400
[SNORTS]
Higher! Higher!

159
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:31,520
[♪♪♪]

160
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:34,039
[LAUGHING]

161
00:06:34,039 --> 00:06:36,719
[DADDY PIG SNORTING
AND LAUGHING]

162
00:06:36,719 --> 00:06:39,479
NARRATOR
Daddy pig flies the kite
very well.

163
00:06:41,840 --> 00:06:43,799
Wow!
Wow!

164
00:06:43,799 --> 00:06:46,880
DADDY
Yes I am a bit of an expert
at these things.

165
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:49,080
[♪♪♪]

166
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:52,120
Watch out
for the trees!

167
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,080
You might get the kite
stuck in one.

168
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:57,039
Don't worry.
I know what I'm doing.

169
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:03,640
NARRATOR
Oh, dear. Daddy Pig has got
the kite caught in a tree.

170
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:05,719
Oh, no.
[SNORTS]

171
00:07:08,919 --> 00:07:11,400
Hm.
Oh.

172
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:14,400
[CRYING]

173
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:17,960
MOMMY PIG:
Don't worry George.
Daddy will get the kite down.

174
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:20,520
Hooray!
[SNORTS AND GIGGLES]

175
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:22,840
Uh, yes.

176
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,280
[GIGGLES]

177
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,799
Careful! There's
a big muddy puddle.

178
00:07:26,799 --> 00:07:29,520
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George love to jump
in muddy puddles.

179
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:31,200
Can we jump
in the puddle?

180
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,640
Please?

181
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:35,680
No. I don't want you
covered in mud.

182
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:37,400
Oh...

183
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:40,440
Stand back, children.

184
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:42,840
Please be careful, Daddy pig.
[SNORTS]

185
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:46,000
[SNORTS]
I know what I'm doing.

186
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,200
[♪♪♪]

187
00:07:50,159 --> 00:07:52,719
[BRANCH CREAKS]

188
00:07:52,719 --> 00:07:54,640
Please be careful. 

189
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,520
[KIDS LAUGHING]

190
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:59,719
Just a bit further,
Daddy! Ha, ha!

191
00:08:01,159 --> 00:08:02,840
Daddy Pig, you are much

192
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:04,760
too heavy for that branch.
[BRANCH CREAKS]

193
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:06,200
[SNORTS]
Nonsense.

194
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:08,960
I know exactly
how heavy I am.

195
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:10,719
[SNORTS]
There.

196
00:08:10,719 --> 00:08:12,159
Hooray!

197
00:08:12,159 --> 00:08:14,719
NARRATOR
Daddy Pig has rescued
the kite.

198
00:08:14,719 --> 00:08:16,039
Whoa!

199
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:21,400
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear. Everyone is
covered in mud.

200
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:23,200
[LAUGHS, SNORTS]

201
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:24,400
It's only mud.

202
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:27,640
[ALL LAUGHING]

203
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:30,280
NARRATOR:
Luckily, Daddy Pig
hasn't hurt himself.

204
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:32,520
And the kite
is out of the tree.

205
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:35,880
[IN UNISON]
Hooray! Ha-ha-ha!

206
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:38,919
[SNORTS]
Mommy, now that
we're all muddy,

207
00:08:38,919 --> 00:08:40,600
can we jump
in the puddle?

208
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:44,959
[SNORTS]
I suppose so. After all,
you can't get any muddier.

209
00:08:44,959 --> 00:08:47,360
[LAUGHING, SNORTS]

210
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:50,120
And I think Daddy Pig is going
to be doing the washing.

211
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,760
Oh...
[SNORTS]

212
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,680
[PEPPA &amp; GEORGE LAUGHING,
SNORTS]

213
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,840
[♪♪♪]

214
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:59,840
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George love jumping
up and down in muddy puddles.

215
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:05,760
Mommy and Daddy love jumping
up and down in muddy puddles.

216
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:09,040
Everyone loves jumping
up and down in muddy puddles.

217
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:11,199
[ALL LAUGHING AND SNORTING]

218
00:09:11,199 --> 00:09:13,000
Jumping up and down
in muddy puddles

219
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,280
is just as much fun
as flying the kite.

220
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:20,760
[♪♪♪]

221
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:25,079
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

222
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,360
[LAUGHING]

223
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:30,000
NARRATOR
It is a lovely
bright, sunny day.

224
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,520
Peppa and her family
are going for a picnic.

225
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:34,600
Daddy Pig is bringing
the picnic basket.

226
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:39,880
[SNORTS]
Picnic blanket, bread, cheese,
tomatoes and lemonade.

227
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:42,199
Is there anything
we've forgotten?

228
00:09:42,199 --> 00:09:44,319
[SNORTS]
Mommy's strawberry cake!

229
00:09:44,319 --> 00:09:47,240
Ho, ho,
I was just teasing.

230
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:50,880
Mommy's homemade
strawberry cake is there too.

231
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:51,920
Is everybody ready?

232
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:53,240
Ready!
Ready!
Ready!

233
00:09:53,240 --> 00:09:55,760
[IGNITION STARTING]
Then let's go!

234
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:57,800
[HORN HONKS]

235
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,480
[HORN HONKS]

236
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:02,720
[ALL LAUGH]
[PEPPA SNORTS]

237
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:05,959
This looks like just the spot
for our picnic.

238
00:10:05,959 --> 00:10:08,360
PEPPA, GEORGE, MOMMY PIG:
Hooray! Ha-ha-ha!

239
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:10,400
[LAUGHS, SNORTS]

240
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:13,160
Ah! It's great
to be outdoors.

241
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:15,720
We should run around a bit
and get some exercise.

242
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:18,360
[SNORTS]
I want to eat,
then have a nap.

243
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:20,920
I certainly don't want
to run around.

244
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:23,480
Maybe Daddy should run
around a bit.

245
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:25,439
His tummy is quite big.

246
00:10:25,439 --> 00:10:27,839
My tummy is not big.
[SNORTS]

247
00:10:27,839 --> 00:10:29,839
But later, I will get
some exercise,

248
00:10:29,839 --> 00:10:32,280
even if no one else does.
[LAUGHING]

249
00:10:32,280 --> 00:10:33,839
Let's eat.

250
00:10:33,839 --> 00:10:35,600
Good idea, Mommy Pig.

251
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:37,680
I'm really hungry.
[SNORTS]

252
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:38,880
[ALL MUNCHING]

253
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:40,839
Mm, delicious!

254
00:10:40,839 --> 00:10:43,240
[BOTH GIGGLING]

255
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:44,839
[LAUGHS]

256
00:10:44,839 --> 00:10:49,439
Ahh! I feel quite sleepy.

257
00:10:49,439 --> 00:10:52,360
I thought you wanted to run
around a bit, Daddy Pig?

258
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,480
Later...

259
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:56,000
[SNORING]

260
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,520
[♪♪♪]

261
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:01,160
[SNORTS]
Look! There's a little
duck pond.

262
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:03,120
[QUACKS]

263
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:05,959
[SNORTS]
Mommy, can we feed
the ducks?

264
00:11:05,959 --> 00:11:08,760
Yes, you can feed them
the rest of the bread.

265
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:11,680
[BOTH LAUGHING]

266
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:14,680
NARRATOR
Peppa and George love
feeding bread to ducks.

267
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:17,160
[QUACKING]
[CONTINUES LAUGHING]

268
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:23,120
Mommy, I think
they want some more.

269
00:11:23,120 --> 00:11:25,240
That was the last of the bread.

270
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:27,120
I'm sure
they've had enough.

271
00:11:27,120 --> 00:11:31,120
[SNORTS]
Sorry, Mrs. Duck,
we've no more bread.

272
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:34,360
[QUACKING]

273
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,560
NARRATOR
The ducks want more food.

274
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:38,199
[SNORING]

275
00:11:38,199 --> 00:11:41,319
So much for Daddy Pig
and his exercise.

276
00:11:41,319 --> 00:11:44,240
[LAUGHING]
Uh, uh? What?

277
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:46,040
[QUACKING]

278
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:47,439
You lot again.

279
00:11:47,439 --> 00:11:50,480
[SNORTS]
Peppa told you,
there's no more bread.

280
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,959
[QUACKS]
PEPPA: Mommy,

281
00:11:51,959 --> 00:11:54,520
we do have
strawberry cake.

282
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,480
Well, if there's any cake
left over,

283
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:59,120
you can give it to the ducks.
[ALL LAUGHING]

284
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:02,680
NARRATOR:
Everyone likes Mommy Pig's
homemade strawberry cake.

285
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:04,439
[BUZZING]
Ooh! A wasp!

286
00:12:04,439 --> 00:12:06,760
I hate wasps. Shoo!

287
00:12:06,760 --> 00:12:10,480
What a fuss, Mommy Pig.
It's only a little wasp.

288
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,560
[CONTINUES BUZZING]
[GASPS] Go away, wasp!

289
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:14,520
Just stay still, Mommy Pig.

290
00:12:14,520 --> 00:12:16,280
Then it will fly away.
[SNORTS]

291
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:21,199
There! You see,
all you had to was stay still.

292
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:23,920
Eh! Get away!

293
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:26,319
Scram! Whoa!
[SNORTS]

294
00:12:26,319 --> 00:12:29,439
Help! Whoa! Shoo!
[SNORTS]

295
00:12:29,439 --> 00:12:31,360
Get it off me! Whoa!

296
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:34,000
[SNORTS]
I hope the wasp
doesn't sting Daddy.

297
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,680
Whoa! Get away, you little pest!
[SNORTS]

298
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:40,439
No, Daddy Pig is running too
fast for the wasp to catch him.

299
00:12:40,439 --> 00:12:42,319
Whoa!
[SNORTS]

300
00:12:42,319 --> 00:12:46,079
Let's eat our cake before
the wasp comes back.

301
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,599
[ALL MUNCHING]

302
00:12:48,599 --> 00:12:50,280
[♪♪♪]

303
00:12:50,280 --> 00:12:51,680
[DUCK QUACKS]

304
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:55,240
Oh, no! We forgot to leave
any for the ducks.

305
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:58,079
[PANTING]

306
00:12:58,079 --> 00:12:59,400
I think I lost it.

307
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:01,240
[SNORTS]
You said you would
run around

308
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:02,839
and get some exercise,
Daddy Pig.

309
00:13:02,839 --> 00:13:05,280
But I didn't believe
you'd do it.

310
00:13:05,280 --> 00:13:07,120
[KIDS LAUGH]

311
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,760
[LAUGHS, SNORTS]

312
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:12,760
Luckily, I managed to hang on
to my slice of strawberry cake.

313
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:14,400
PEPPA:
Stop, Daddy!

314
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:17,439
We promised the rest
of the cake for the ducks.

315
00:13:17,439 --> 00:13:19,839
Oh...

316
00:13:19,839 --> 00:13:24,160
You are very lucky ducks.
[QUACKING, MUNCHING]

317
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:26,400
Say thank you to
Daddy Pig.

318
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:27,719
[QUACKS]

319
00:13:27,719 --> 00:13:31,280
You're most welcome,
ho, ho!

320
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:34,520
It's time to go home.
Say goodbye to the ducks.

321
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:37,120
Bye, bye, ducks.
[QUACKING]

322
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:40,240
[SNORTS]
See you next time! Hee-hee!

323
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:42,280
[ALL LAUGHING, SNORTING]

324
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:44,560
[CAR HORN HONKS]

325
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:46,640
[QUACKING]

326
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:51,760
[♪♪♪]

327
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:56,439
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

328
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:02,360
NARRATOR:
Mommy Pig and Daddy Pig
have been tidying the house.

329
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,880
[RATTLES]
[SNORTS]

330
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:07,000
Mommy Pig and I found
this old box in the attic.

331
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,120
[BLOWS]

332
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,319
Ooh!
Ooh!

333
00:14:09,319 --> 00:14:11,439
Can anyone guess
what's inside?

334
00:14:11,439 --> 00:14:14,280
Hm, nope.
[SNORTS]

335
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:16,479
It's full of
musical instruments.

336
00:14:16,479 --> 00:14:17,599
[ACCORDION PLAYS NOTE]

337
00:14:17,599 --> 00:14:19,040
[IN UNISON]
Wow!

338
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:20,760
[DADDY PIG LAUGHS, SNORTS]

339
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,760
They are a bit old and dusty.

340
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:23,839
[BLOWS]

341
00:14:23,839 --> 00:14:28,079
[SNEEZES]
[ALL LAUGH]

342
00:14:28,079 --> 00:14:31,520
[SNORTS]
This is the violin I used
to play when I was little.

343
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:34,360
Mommy?
Can you play your violin?

344
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:36,880
I haven't played it
for a long time.

345
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:39,199
Please, Mommy!
Please play it!

346
00:14:39,199 --> 00:14:40,360
[SNORTS]

347
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:42,839
I hope
I haven't forgotten how.

348
00:14:42,839 --> 00:14:44,920
[PLAYING SLOW TUNE]

349
00:14:48,479 --> 00:14:49,800
Bravo!
[ALL CLAPPING]

350
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:51,319
Hooray! Hee-hee!

351
00:14:51,319 --> 00:14:52,599
[SNORTS]

352
00:14:52,599 --> 00:14:55,000
Mommy?
Can I play the violin?

353
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,920
Hold it like this.

354
00:14:56,920 --> 00:14:58,479
Yes, Mommy.

355
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,439
[PLAYS SCREECHY TUNE]

356
00:15:02,040 --> 00:15:03,240
Oh!
Oh!

357
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:04,839
NARRATOR:
Oh, dear.

358
00:15:04,839 --> 00:15:07,680
I do not think it
is meant to sound like that.

359
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:10,240
[SNORTS]
George wants to try.

360
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:13,160
Hold it like this, George.
[SNORTS]

361
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:15,839
[PLAYING SCREECHY NOTES]

362
00:15:15,839 --> 00:15:17,680
Oh!
Oh!
Oh!

363
00:15:17,680 --> 00:15:19,719
NARRATOR:
That does not sound right
either.

364
00:15:19,719 --> 00:15:22,479
The violin
is too hard to play.

365
00:15:22,479 --> 00:15:23,880
Peppa...
[SNORTS]

366
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:25,920
...maybe you would do better
with this tin drum.

367
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,880
[SNORTS]
Thank you, Daddy.

368
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,880
[PLAYING DRUM]
NARRATOR: That sounds better.

369
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:32,319
Peppa loves
playing the drum.

370
00:15:32,319 --> 00:15:36,160
Ho, ho! Lovely.
Yes, it sounds very nice.

371
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,760
[CONTINUES PLAYING DRUM]

372
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:40,760
This is Daddy Pig's
old accordion.

373
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:44,439
I used to play this to Mommy Pig
when we first met.

374
00:15:44,439 --> 00:15:46,360
[PLAYS ROMANTIC MELODY]

375
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:50,719
Oh, Daddy Pig.
I remember this tune.

376
00:15:50,719 --> 00:15:53,079
[PLAYS DRUM, LAUGHS]
[SNORTS]

377
00:15:53,079 --> 00:15:56,120
[LAUGHS]
[LAUGHS, SNORTS]

378
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:58,479
NARRATOR:
George wants to play
the accordion too.

379
00:15:58,479 --> 00:16:00,160
Are you sure, George?
[SNORTS]

380
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:02,240
The accordion
is quite difficult.

381
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:05,280
George ,the a-cro-dion

382
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:08,319
is almost as difficult
to play as my drum.

383
00:16:08,319 --> 00:16:09,520
[THWACK]

384
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:10,760
[SNORTS]

385
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,160
Okay, George.

386
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:13,880
[GIGGLING]

387
00:16:13,880 --> 00:16:15,959
[PLAYING OFF-KEY TUNE]

388
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,880
Oh.

389
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:22,000
NARRATOR
Maybe George is a bit too
little to play the accordion.

390
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,319
Daddy?
[SNORTS]

391
00:16:23,319 --> 00:16:26,400
What other instruments
are in the box?

392
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:27,920
Just this horn.

393
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,680
[SNORTS]
Can I try?

394
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:31,760
You have to blow it
very hard.

395
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,000
[INHALES]

396
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,359
[BLOWS RASPBERRY]

397
00:16:35,359 --> 00:16:37,479
NARRATOR
That does not sound right.

398
00:16:37,479 --> 00:16:39,359
[SNORTS]
It's impossible!

399
00:16:39,359 --> 00:16:42,640
[SNORTS]
I think I used to be able
to play it.

400
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:43,839
[INHALES]

401
00:16:43,839 --> 00:16:45,319
[BLOWS RASPBERRY]

402
00:16:45,319 --> 00:16:47,599
NARRATOR:
That really does not sound
right.

403
00:16:47,599 --> 00:16:52,520
[LAUGHING]
Maybe it just needs someone
big and strong like me.

404
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:54,120
[INHALES]

405
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:56,199
[BLOWING RASPBERRY]

406
00:16:59,040 --> 00:17:01,400
NARRATOR:
That does not sound right
either.

407
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:03,199
[PANTS]

408
00:17:03,199 --> 00:17:04,359
Peppa's right,

409
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:06,639
it is impossible to play.

410
00:17:06,639 --> 00:17:09,960
Never mind, Daddy Pig.
Just stick to the accordion.

411
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:12,159
[SNORTS]
You play it beautifully.

412
00:17:12,159 --> 00:17:15,399
Ho, ho! Well, I do
play it quite nicely,

413
00:17:15,399 --> 00:17:17,359
even if I say so myself.

414
00:17:17,359 --> 00:17:19,560
And I'll play my violin.

415
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:21,560
And I will play my drum.

416
00:17:21,560 --> 00:17:23,399
NARRATOR:
Mommy Pig plays the violin.

417
00:17:23,399 --> 00:17:24,680
[PLAYING SLOW TUNE]

418
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:26,760
Daddy Pig
plays the accordion.

419
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:28,000
[PLAYING ROMANTIC TUNE]

420
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,240
Peppa plays the drum.

421
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:31,360
[PLAYING SIMPLE TUNE]

422
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:34,480
But what instrument
will George play?

423
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:36,560
[PIGS CONTINUE PLAYING MUSIC]

424
00:17:38,159 --> 00:17:40,159
[HORN BLASTS]

425
00:17:41,399 --> 00:17:42,919
[HORN BLASTS]

426
00:17:42,919 --> 00:17:44,080
[LAUGHING]

427
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:46,480
George is blowing the horn!

428
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:51,000
Mommy couldn't play the horn
and Daddy couldn't play it.

429
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,320
And even I couldn't play it.

430
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:55,879
[SNORTS]
But George can play it!

431
00:17:55,879 --> 00:17:57,320
[GIGGLES, SNORTS]

432
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,200
[HORN BLASTS]

433
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:01,399
[BIRDS TWEETING]

434
00:18:01,399 --> 00:18:03,120
[HORN BLASTS]

435
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:05,280
[PIGS PLAYING
MUSICAL INSTRUMENTS]

436
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:14,800
[HORN BLASTS]

437
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,879
[LAUGHING]

438
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,080
[♪♪♪]

439
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:22,120
[GIGGLES, SNORTS]

440
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:23,800
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

441
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:25,800
[SNORTS, GIGGLES]

442
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:26,800
[SNORTS]

443
00:18:26,800 --> 00:18:28,520
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

444
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:30,840
[SNORTS, LAUGHS]

445
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:32,800
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

446
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,639
[SNORTS, GIGGLES]

